  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Child Protection System to Keep Filipino Children Safe Online (SaferKidsPH)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SaferKidsPH supports the Philippine government in raising public awareness on child online safety, improving capacity of police and courts to detect, investigate and prosecute cases of online sexual abuse and exploitation of children (OSAEC), and ensuring that quality support services are accessible for vulnerable children and families. SaferKidsPH is aligned with Australia and Philippines&#x2019; shared commitments to protect children from all forms of abuse and exploitation. Program delivery partners are the Australian Federal Police, and the consortium of UNICEF, Save the Children Philippines, and The Asia Foundation. It works with government, civil society, and other like-minded donors and development partners. It engages with children, families, communities,  schools, and private sector.</narrative>
  </description>
